  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2026-01-03T09:35:19.057Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "As a group owner I find the ability to drop a pedestal for my group and partner groups incredibly helpful.  This allows for an open invite for people in my instances to be able to join my group or partner groups easily.  \n\nWhile this feature is incredibly useful there are some minor problems.  Some users see our authorized group pedestals and feel the need to add their own unrelated groups which leads to a cluttered and confusing group of pedestals that have nothing to do with our group.  \n\nAdding the ability for groups to limit group pedestals to moderators and having settings in the group permissions would allow this feature to be more granular and usable for group instances.  Group moderators would no longer have to clean up the portal sprawl that sometimes collects next to the authorized group pedestals.",
